        "summary": "Isabel Schnabel, Executive Board member of the European Central Bank (ECB), will leave the ECB early to take a senior role at the International Monetary Fund (IMF). She has been selected as director of the monetary and capital markets department, where she will start on Jan 4. Her early departure adds urgency to the 2027 leadership shakeup at the ECB, with President Christine Lagarde and Chief Economist Philip Lane also set to leave. European Union leaders are expected to agree on all three appointments at once, potentially at a summit in December. The IMF's Managing Director, Kristalina Georgieva, commended Schnabel's ability to promote global monetary and financial stability and foster international collaboration. Her departure raises pressure on Germany to decide what it wants at the EU.",
