        "summary": "Azerbaijan has attracted strong interest from foreign companies in renewable energy projects, according to SOCAR Green CEO Elmir Musayev at the 2nd Azerbaijan International Investment Forum in Baku. He noted that experts have assessed over 200 gigawatts of solar energy potential and 157 gigawatts worth of offshore wind technical potential, with around 35 gigawatts considered economically viable. Musayov also highlighted the first phase of renewable energy development, supported by a 250-megawatt/2-hour battery energy storage system. He said that the cost of capital had increased after the US Federal Reserve raised interest rates, making it more difficult for companies like SOCAR to finance projects. Currently, financing in Azerbaijan mainly comes from international financial institutions (IFIs) as projects require long-term financing, typically 15–20 years.",
        "shortSummary": "Azerbaijan attracts strong interest from foreign companies in renewable energy projects, with significant potential for both solar and offshore wind energy, despite increased costs and financing challenges.",
